  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result 4 [exact].** t₂(u) = ∏_s g_s(u) · tr[ℒ⁽²⁾₁(u)⋯ℒ⁽²⁾_L(u) · ∧²G] equals the quantum-minor t₂ identically at L = 2, 4 sites for companion, diagonal, generic and trivial twist (two u values each). One-pass vector form (6×6 aux grid) agrees with the matrix at L = 4 to 2·10⁻¹⁶. (Per Paul, no L = 6 test for t₂.)\n\n**All three transfer matrices now have a one-pass vector form:** t₁ (aux 4, shifts 0), t₂ (aux ∧² = 6, F shifted by h), t₃ (aux ∧³ ≅ 4̄, A by −h, F by +3h).",
